WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:07.509 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  with the end of year four coming along  and season 11 on the horizon The  Division II team at massive  entertainment have released a public  test server or pts to let us try and  break some of the new additions coming  in season 11. year 5 will be bringing us  some new seasons in the new descent game  mode but these aren't being featured in  the pts for now Focus has been placed on  various balances as well as new gear  weapons Exotics and set items I've put a  few hours into testing these out and in  this video I'm going to share my  thoughts around what I've managed to  muck around with so far  before I get into it please remember  that this is a test server it's very  likely that everything I talk about here  will be tweaked and adjusted before the  final release after all this is the  purpose of the PTS  the pts has been going for a few days  now but this is the last update before  year 5 begins so don't be expecting too  much realistically we're receiving one  new brand set one new gear set two new  named items two new named weapons one  new weapon Talent one new exotic weapon  one new exotic item a few PVP quality of  life updates and a growing list of game  performance and other updates  immediately we can see that the focus  has been placed on marksman rifles and  status effects to a lesser extent with  this update  both the brand set and the gear set  provide bonuses to marksman rifles and  headshots  this is pretty standard the last one or  two have been focused on skills so I'm  actually pretty stoked to see some  attention being brought to the sniper  builds however when comparing my current  One-Shot sniper build to this new Hot  Shot gear set after a number of tweaks I  actually wasn't getting very high  numbers  I would say that this is a much easier  way to build high damage snipers and the  extra armor is useful but I think I  prefer my original build to what this  new set is offering like I said I expect  we'll see some tweaks here not that I  want this to be the only thing to run  while using a marksman rifle I just like  it to be a little more relevant if I'm  sniping I'm running a glass Cannon to  get the most out of my shots the armor  is nice but at high difficulties with a  low rate of fire this seems a little  redundant  but the new brand set Habsburg guard  there seems to be a little something  different going on here  it starts off similar with headshot  damage and Marksman rifle damage but  then it moves them to status effects  which seems like a weak three-piece  bonus to me  both the new named pieces to the set  also delve into status effects  the chest has a 20 second cooldown so I  don't really see this being too popular  over other options but the backpack  could be interesting with the right  crowd control or status effect build  the sacrum Imperium is the new exotic  variation of the g28 Marksman rifle it  has the talent the Trap summing it up  you can tag up to a maximum of 10  enemies by viewing them in your sights  killing one of the marked targets with a  headshot will apply a 10 second burn  status effect and 50 movement speed  decrease on all other targets  this is interesting but it falls into  the same trap as most of the other  exotic weapons as being a little too  situational and underwhelming to be of  any real use in the long term targets  need to be held in your sights for over  two seconds before they are marked and  when everything is running around and  shooting at you this is a long time  this is really only useful as an ambush  weapon before the hostiles have been  eggrolled but then again it takes so  long to Mark a group that I'm not sure  that I'd bother  however I must say the design of this  weapon is awesome  the new named weapons are the prophet  revolver and The Relic g28 maximum rifle  I absolutely love their perfect talent  but just not on these weapons  killing an enemy with a headshot  guarantees the next shot will be a  critical headshot  if I could put this on the white death  or some other hard-hitting sniper I  would be a very happy man but the  non-perfect version of this Talent is a  little different  after killing an enemy with a headshot  the next shot landed on any enemy will  be a guaranteed headshot  I'm sure people will find a use for this  perhaps when using a controller but for  me the guaranteed critical hit was what  made this Talent stick out  imagine a sniper build where you can  focus on just headshot damage and  critical head damage completely ignoring  critical hit chance  there have been a number of PVP quality  of life changes mainly relating to  skills more specifically gemmers and the  shrapnel trap  I don't play this game for its unique  PVP experience so I can't really comment  on these but one thing that has been an  area of contention across the community  is the addition of a couple of raid  Exotics into the dark Zone loot pool  there are actually three Exotics being  added but the big horn is already  available outside the raids  I didn't realize how divided the  community really was around this until I  stumbled across a couple of long threads  that were getting very heated  I can actually see the argument from  both sides but I'm not really that  passionate about either I agree there  should be some unique rewards for those  who complete the raid  but if that's all it was people would  only complete the raid once anyway there  is obviously something else raid players  are gaining from completing this game  mode  I'm someone who doesn't have all the  raid Exotics not through a lack of  trying it's just very difficult for me  to find a team of seven other players to  run through it they're able to work with  my difficult time zone but at the same  time I'm really not that worried about  missing out on a couple of different  weapons  the addition of these two weapons into  the dark Zone likely won't impact how  often I frequent the area  regardless of how small this update is  there is one thing that I'm very much  looking forward to the ninja bike  messenger bag exotic backpack  those of you who played through the  division one should remember this it was  the most sought after exotic in the game  at one stage before classified six came  along and ruined all the build diversity  this piece of gear acts as a filler to  complete the requirements towards  unlocking gear set bonuses the reason  this is a game changer is that it can be  used to complete requirements for more  than one set at a time while only taking  up one slot  this will mean that we're able to unlock  more bonuses than we've been able to up  until now it essentially opens up a  whole new tier of build options  unfortunately this isn't available in  the pts but expect to see a huge number  of build videos coming up from YouTubers  in the future as they redefine all of  your favorite builds  I'm not sure how long this pts goes for  or if we'll be seeing multiple different  tiers like we've seen in different ones  but if I had to guess I'd say this won't  be a long one March marks the end of  year four so they'll be wanting to have  everything sorted well before then  I need to repeat what I said earlier  everything I've shown here is subject to  change while this gives a good  indication of what is to come individual  talents and specs are likely to be  adjusted following the end of the PTS  I hope you found this video useful and  I'll catch you in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Music]

